        "raw": "<p>Hiya!</p><p>(the backstory)</p><p>Just got back from Who&#39;s Yer Con in Indianapolis and had a blast. Previously, I had heard about SotM from a person about 6 months ago at a gaming cafe called Arsenal (also in Indy). Lo and behold, the game was being played pretty often. Now neither I nor my fiancee got to actually join in, but in watching others play, we totally got stoked, excited, and I basically ran to the vendor hall and purchased the core game, RC, IR, and a single Ambuscade deck. I even chatted with one of the people who runs games every 4th Tuesday at Arsenal. I think he said he might have even been a frequent poster here on this forum.</p><p>We finally got to actually play last night and had a blast, even though the rulebooks didn&#39;t say anything about what to do when a deck ran out of cards. (That might be a typo, can you guys look into it?) EIther way, we had a blast learning how to play for real, and I immediately wanted to know what was up with Unity (a deck I didn&#39;t seem to have) so I hopped on the internet and ended up in the game store here for &gt;G.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(The setup)</p><p>I went into the store and basically clicked on every damn thing that said it was for sale, and I didn&#39;t currently have. Saw a new set called Shattered Timelines, saw some promo expansion decks that sounded cool, some oversized decks, all kind of stuff. Basically I just threw cash repeatedly at the screen until I realized I had to actually punch in my shipping and google wallet info, and hit purchase to make anything happen. So I did, and aimed for the Fed-Ex two-day shipping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(The problem)</p><p>After lurking on the forums here for an hour or two, I am no longer sure if those items are actually &#39;for sale&#39; or if they are pre-orders or what. I&#39;m under the impression that I&quot;m buying a bunch of brand new stuff when it&#39;s possible that the Kickstarter orders havent&#39; even shipped, and I&#39;m no longer sure if I will get this stufff by the weekend, or if I just need to be patient, or if it might be a month or so.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(The summary)</p><p>I just bought some $100+ worth of awesome &gt;G SotM stuff, and now I&#39;m not sure if it will come in this week, or even this month, due to the kickstarter for the new stuff finishing relatively recently, and the poor &gt;G staff being stuck having to get out all the Kickstarter-related shipping out first. Anyone know how it will work or if I am worrying unreasonably like a jerk?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PS. Thanks to the website, i was able to find out that you&#39;re supposed to shuffle the trash into the deck if you&#39;re ever supposed to draw a card and there aren&#39;t any. Which made Wagner Mars Base&#39;s &quot;Self Destruct Sequence&quot; not a game ender. Yay!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PPS. Thanks for having an awesome game... rare are the games that I will think about buying only after seeing played for a short amount of time.</p>",
